---
import LegalPage from '../../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import LegalOwner from '../../../components/legal/LegalOwner.astro';
import {
  BLINDNOTE_ANALYTICS_RETENTION,
  BLINDNOTE_DELETION_TERM,
  BLINDNOTE_MIN_AGE,
  BLINDNOTE_OWNER,
  LEGAL_EMAIL,
  SPAIN_DIGITAL_CONSENT_AGE,
} from '../../../lib/legal';
import { route } from '../../../i18n';
---
<LegalPage
  lang="en"
  routeKey="blindnotePrivacy"
  title="BlindNote Privacy Policy | Kuxar Studio"
  heading="BlindNote Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy of the BlindNote app: what stays on your phone, AdMob ads, optional Firebase statistics, legal basis, retention periods and your rights."
  updated="26 November 2026"
>
  <p>This policy explains what data is processed by <strong>BlindNote</strong>, the Android music quiz where you pass the phone around in turns to guess the artist, title and year of the song playing in Spotify. We wrote it to be understood: if anything is unclear, write to us.</p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>BlindNote has no accounts, sign-up or rankings, and no servers of its own.</li>
    <li>Notification access is only used to see and control the music in the Spotify app. BlindNote does not read, store or send your notifications.</li>
    <li>The songs being played and the players' names never leave your phone.</li>
    <li>The app shows Google AdMob ads. Where the law requires it, you are asked for consent first.</li>
    <li>Usage statistics and crash reports are off until you accept them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <LegalOwner owner={BLINDNOTE_OWNER} lang="en" />

  <h2>2. What data we process, why and on what legal basis</h2>
  <table class="legal-table" tabindex="0">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Title, artist and Spotify track identifier of the song being played, which the app sees thanks to notification access. <strong>Only on your phone.</strong></td>
        <td>Act as the referee: skip to another song, start it, pause it and check that it belongs to the chosen theme.</td>
        <td>Provision of the service you ask for (Art. 6(1)(b)). You also grant the Android permission.</td>
        <td>Not stored: used in the phone's memory and never sent.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Player names and scores. <strong>Only on your phone.</strong></td>
        <td>Run the game and show the result.</td>
        <td>Provision of the service (Art. 6(1)(b)).</td>
        <td>Until the app is closed. Not stored or sent.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Settings: your answer about the statistics, the language and your choice about ads. <strong>Only on your phone.</strong></td>
        <td>Remember your preferences and your consent decisions.</td>
        <td>Provision of the service (Art. 6(1)(b)) and legal obligation to respect your consent (Art. 6(1)(c)).</td>
        <td>Until you clear the app's data or uninstall it. Not included in backups.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Technical data that Google receives when the consent tool (User Messaging Platform) is checked, such as the IP address and the type of device.</td>
        <td>Find out whether you have to be asked for consent to ads in your country and remember your answer.</td>
        <td>Compliance with legal obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)) and legitimate interest in being able to prove it (Art. 6(1)(f)).</td>
        <td>Your answer is stored on the phone. What Google receives, under Google's privacy policy.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Ad data (Google AdMob): IP address (from which an approximate location can be inferred), interactions with the app and the ads, diagnostic and performance data, Android advertising ID and app set ID.</td>
        <td>Show an ad before the result of a game to fund the app, measure it and prevent fraud.</td>
        <td><strong>Your consent</strong> where required (Art. 6(1)(a)); otherwise, legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)).</td>
        <td>The periods in Google's privacy policy.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Usage statistics (Google Analytics for Firebase): the events in section 4, Analytics' automatic events, technical data (app version, model, language, system and approximate location inferred from the IP address) and pseudonymous installation identifiers.</td>
        <td>Learn how the app is used and improve it.</td>
        <td><strong>Your consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a)). Only collected if you accept.</td>
        <td>{BLINDNOTE_ANALYTICS_RETENTION.en} for data linked to identifiers. Totals without identifiers may be kept longer.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Crash reports (Firebase Crashlytics): technical state of the app and device at the time of the crash, model, system, version and random installation and session identifiers.</td>
        <td>Detect and fix crashes.</td>
        <td><strong>Your consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a)). Only sent if you accept.</td>
        <td>Google states 90 days before it starts removing them. The Firebase installation ID is kept until its deletion is requested; Google then removes it within 180 days.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>BlindNote does not sell your data or give it to anyone else, unless required by law, and does not build profiles that affect you.</p>

  <h2>3. What stays on your phone</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Notification access.</strong> Android requires this permission for one app to see and control the music of another. The permission is broader than BlindNote needs: the system describes it as access to all notifications. BlindNote uses it only to find the playback session of the Spotify app and to pause it, resume it or skip to the next song. The app component that receives this access is empty: it does not read, store or send any notification, not even those from Spotify. You can withdraw the permission at any time in the system settings; the game cannot be played without it.</li>
    <li><strong>Song being played.</strong> During a game, BlindNote sees the title, artist and identifier of the song playing in Spotify and compares them with a list included in the app itself. They are only used in the phone's memory: they are not stored, not sent and not part of the statistics.</li>
    <li><strong>Player names and scores.</strong> They are used during the game and erased when the app is closed.</li>
    <li><strong>Installed apps.</strong> BlindNote checks whether the Spotify app is installed. It does not look for any other app and does not send the result.</li>
    <li><strong>Settings.</strong> They are stored in the app's private storage and are not moved to another device through backups.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Spotify.</strong> To play you need the Spotify app installed on your phone. It is your own, independent app, not a provider of ours: BlindNote does not play music, does not use Spotify's sign-in, SDK or API, has no access to your account and receives no data from Spotify over the internet. When you open a playlist you move to the Spotify app, which has <a href="https://www.spotify.com/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">its own privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>4. Statistics and crash reports: your choice</h2>
  <p>When you open BlindNote for the first time, we ask whether you want to share usage statistics and crash reports. <strong>They are off by default</strong> and the app works the same if you decline. If you accept, Google Analytics for Firebase and Firebase Crashlytics are used. These are the events BlindNote sends:</p>
  <table class="legal-table" tabindex="0">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Event</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Accompanying data</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>permission_shown</code></td><td>The permission screen was shown</td><td>None</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>permission_granted</code></td><td>The permission was granted</td><td>None</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>permission_abandoned</code></td><td>The screen was left without granting it</td><td>None</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>game_started</code></td><td>A game started</td><td>Theme, number of players, rounds and seconds per turn</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>game_finished</code></td><td>A game ended</td><td>None</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>game_abandoned</code></td><td>A game was abandoned</td><td>None</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>skip_failed</code></td><td>The song could not be changed</td><td>None</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>unknown_song</code></td><td>A song outside the theme was played</td><td>None (only counted)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>prepare_failed</code></td><td>The music could not be prepared</td><td>None</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ad_detected</code></td><td>Spotify was playing an ad</td><td>None (only counted)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Google Analytics also records <strong>automatic events</strong>, for example: first open, session start, time of use, screen shown, app or system update, data cleared, app removed, app crash and ad activity. The <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/9234069" rel="noopener">full list</a> is on Google's website.</p>
  <p>These tools do not receive titles, artists, player names or notifications. Google assigns <strong>pseudonymous identifiers</strong>, generated at random, to the installation (Analytics instance ID, Firebase installation ID and Crashlytics ID). We do not use them to find out who you are, but they tell one installation from another. In BlindNote, Analytics has the collection of the advertising ID and ad personalisation turned off.</p>
  <p><strong>How to withdraw consent:</strong> in <strong>Settings &gt; Usage statistics</strong>. From then on no more data is sent, the Analytics identifier is reset on the phone and pending crash reports are deleted. What was already sent is kept for the periods in section 2. Withdrawing consent does not affect processing carried out before.</p>

  <h2>5. Ads and the consent message</h2>
  <p>BlindNote may show one full-screen ad before the result of a game, using Google Mobile Ads (AdMob).</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consent.</strong> When the app opens, Google's consent tool (User Messaging Platform) connects to Google to find out whether you have to be asked in your country, and stores your answer on the phone.</li>
    <li><strong>When ads are requested.</strong> Each time you open the app, BlindNote refreshes your situation with that tool and only requests ads if the tool authorises it: if you have already answered the message, even if your answer was to refuse, or if you do not have to be asked. If your answer is needed and you have not given it yet, no ad is requested. If the refresh fails (for example, with no connection) or the message cannot be loaded or shown, <strong>the decision the tool stored in an earlier session may be reused</strong>; if it stored none, no ads are requested.</li>
    <li><strong>Which ads.</strong> Depending on your answer, Google may show personalised, non-personalised or limited ads, or none. If you change your choice, BlindNote discards any ad it had ready and checks with the tool again. If there is no ad, the game simply continues.</li>
    <li><strong>How to change your choice.</strong> Where applicable, in <strong>Settings &gt; Ad privacy</strong> inside BlindNote. You can also reset or delete the advertising ID in the Android settings.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Ad data is encrypted in transit and Google uses it for advertising, analytics and fraud prevention. It may share it with the advertising partners listed in the consent message. More information: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses data from apps that use its services</a> and <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure" rel="noopener">data collected by the ads SDK</a>.</p>

  <h2>6. Providers</h2>
  <p>The only provider is <strong>Google Ireland Limited</strong>, together with the companies of its group:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics for Firebase and Firebase Crashlytics:</strong> Google acts as a processor on our behalf (<a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy in Firebase</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>Google AdMob and User Messaging Platform:</strong> Google also acts as an independent controller, under the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google privacy policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Spotify is not a provider of ours: it is an independent app that you have installed (see section 3).</p>

  <h2>7. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Google may process data outside the European Economic Area, with the safeguards described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy/frameworks" rel="noopener">its data transfer frameworks</a> (Art. 46 GDPR).</p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can exercise your rights of <strong>access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction of processing and portability</strong> at any time, and withdraw your consent, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a>. We reply within {BLINDNOTE_DELETION_TERM.en} at most. As there are no accounts and we do not know who uses the app, we may not be able to link the data kept by Google to you; if so, we will tell you. You can also contact <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google</a> directly.</p>
  <p>If you believe we have not handled your request properly, you can lodge a complaint with the <strong>Spanish Data Protection Agency</strong> (<a href="https://www.aepd.es" rel="noopener">aepd.es</a>) or with the authority of your country.</p>

  <h2>9. Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>BlindNote has no accounts, so there is no account to delete. To remove everything: turn off <strong>Settings &gt; Usage statistics</strong> if you had accepted them, uninstall the app, revoke notification access if it is still granted and reset the advertising ID. We explain it step by step on the <a href={route('blindnoteDelete', 'en')}>data deletion page</a>.</p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>BlindNote is not directed at children under {BLINDNOTE_MIN_AGE} and does not knowingly ask them for data. If you are below the age at which your country allows you to consent to data processing ({SPAIN_DIGITAL_CONSENT_AGE} in Spain; up to 16 in other countries), do not accept the statistics or personalised ads without your parent or guardian. If you believe a child has given us data, write to <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a>.</p>

  <h2>11. Security</h2>
  <p>Data sent to Google is encrypted in transit. BlindNote does not allow unencrypted connections, keeps its settings in the app's private storage and excludes them from backups. If a security breach affecting your data occurred, we would notify the Spanish Data Protection Agency within 72 hours and, if it posed a high risk to you, we would also notify you.</p>

  <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If the app or the way data is processed changes, we will update this page and its date. If the change is significant, we will announce it in the app and, where needed, ask for your consent again.</p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>For any privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
  <p><small>Compatible with Spotify; not affiliated. Spotify is a trademark of Spotify AB. Google, Android, AdMob and Firebase are trademarks of Google LLC.</small></p>
</LegalPage>
